        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(qa): canonicalize channel routing scenarios",
        "body": "Closes #101073\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where channel canary and routing QA behavior was duplicated across transport-specific imperative runners, allowing Telegram, Slack, WhatsApp, Matrix, QA Channel, and Crabline coverage to drift.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds seven canonical YAML/shared-flow scenarios for channel canary, DM/group routing, mention gating, sender allowlist block/override, top-level reply shape, secondary conversation isolation, and multi-actor ordering. Selected scenario IDs now reach the shared transport factory so QA Channel, Crabline, and live adapters configure the same behavior contract. Matrix's replaced imperative catalog owners and direct tests are removed after live parity; unrelated command, thread, restart/config, media, lifecycle, provider, and runtime scenarios remain unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA operators can run the same channel routing contract through the canonical `qa suite` host across normalized and live transports. Live adapter defaults select the canonical scenarios, and Matrix routing evidence now covers DM, primary/secondary rooms, mention gates, allowlists, reply shape, and actor ordering without duplicate imperative owners.\n\nAI-assisted change. I understand the implementation and reviewed the transport/config ownership boundaries. No agent transcript is attached because explicit approval to publish sanitized session logs was not requested before creation.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- QA Channel: all seven canonical scenarios passed.\n- Crabline Telegram: `channel-canary` and `channel-mention-gating` passed.\n- Matrix live adapter: canary, DM/group routing, mention gating, sender allowlist, top-level reply shape, secondary isolation, and multi-actor ordering passed on Blacksmith Testbox.\n- Focused remote suites: QA catalog/transport/suite and Matrix catalog/runtime/config/sync tests passed after migration; Matrix sync regression covers per-room cursors.\n- Broad gate: `pnpm check:changed` passed on Testbox `tbx_01kww83en3pjz27dh7g12njwk4` (types, lint, import cycles, guards).\n- Review: `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --stream-engine-output` completed clean with no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
